  "notes": "Digitized from official Opus 5 launch figures via scripts/digitize_chart.py. Effort curves (Frontier-Bench v0.1, GDPval-AA v2): geometric marker centroids on log-cost axes (source_type digitized_chart). Opus 4.8 is drawn BLUE on these charts (unlike gold in the Sonnet 5 pilot); recovered via a new 'blue' SERIES_COLORS entry added to scripts/digitize_chart.py. GPT-5.6 Sol is drawn light-gray, sharing its hue with vertical gridlines; recovered via density-peak blob discrimination (filled marker discs vs thin gridline strokes) with a widened gray window and lower min_count. GDPval-AA v2 y-axis is a broken linear scale, calibrated only on its 1200-1900 Elo region. GPT-5.6 Sol has only 4 points (not 5) on the GDPval-AA v2 chart -- its effort ladder stops before 'max'; not fabricated. Misaligned behavior: printed bar labels (labeled_value_read), see digitized/anthropic-opus5-misaligned-behavior.json. See digitized/*.json for asset hashes, axis calibration, dual-read error estimates.",
